# Atlas — leave policies, requests, balances (Sprint 06)
# Login first (see auth.http) and paste the bearer token below.
# You also need a worker id — hire one via workers.http and paste it in.

@host = http://localhost:5000
@token = PASTE_TOKEN_HERE
@workerId = PASTE_WORKER_ID

### Define the org's leave policy for the US (org admin only) → 201
# 24 days/year, up to 10 carried into the next year. USA statutory minimum is 0.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/leave-policies
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "country": "USA",
  "annualEntitlementDays": 24,
  "carryoverCapDays": 10
}

### Below the statutory minimum → 422 (the message names the country's floor)
# Germany's illustrative minimum is 20 days; 10 is refused.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/leave-policies
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "country": "DEU",
  "annualEntitlementDays": 10,
  "carryoverCapDays": 5
}

### List the org's leave policies
GET {{host}}/api/v1/leave-policies
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Submit a leave request for a worker (HR/admin on behalf, v1) → 201
# Mon–Fri in September = 5 working days (weekends don't count; no holiday calendars yet).
POST {{host}}/api/v1/leave-requests
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "workerId": "{{workerId}}",
  "from": "2026-09-07",
  "to": "2026-09-11",
  "note": "Family visit"
}

### Approve it → 200 (checks balance as of the leave's start + no overlap)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/leave-requests/PASTE_REQUEST_ID/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Deny a different request → 200
POST {{host}}/api/v1/leave-requests/PASTE_REQUEST_ID/deny
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Cancel a submitted or approved request → 200
POST {{host}}/api/v1/leave-requests/PASTE_REQUEST_ID/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Overdraw the balance: approving more than accrued → 422
# Early January has barely accrued; a ten-day request there cannot be approved.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/leave-requests
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "workerId": "{{workerId}}",
  "from": "2026-01-05",
  "to": "2026-01-16"
}

### The worker's balance today (derived, never stored)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/workers/{{workerId}}/leave-balance
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ...and as of a chosen date ("what will they have on July 1?")
GET {{host}}/api/v1/workers/{{workerId}}/leave-balance?asOf=2026-07-01
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List leave requests (org-scoped, cursor pagination as everywhere)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/leave-requests?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
